    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="0803" n="1637" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/408</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-26T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 28, 10.18 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4090. The War Trade Board [from Dresel]:</p>
                <p>No. 105. Legation’s 4037, 22d, my 101. Cotton agreement definitely ratified by
                    Swiss Government with restriction stated my 101 and will go into force at once.
                        Dresel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
